title: Genre field editors
intro: The genre components' fields that took lists and names typed from memory have editors now: rows of items, recipes, costs and colors, the next room's hotspots, a difficulty picked from the charts, ticks for a fighter's moves and a compass that can point nowhere.
project: Adventure | Field Kit Two
scene: Kitchen

chapter: Adventures | Items, rooms and lines
select: Kettle
explain: field:UseWith.Gives | Gives | What using the cup on the kettle gives was items and counts typed with commas. Each is a row now: the item picked from what the game gives, and how many.
click: editor:UseWith.Gives:add
choose: UseWith.Gives:item:2:pick = Sardines
editorset: UseWith.Gives:count:2 = 2
expectvalue: Kettle.UseWith.Gives = Tea, Sardines 2
select: Back Door
explain: field:Hotspot.Arrive At | Arrive At | Where the walker comes in, in the next room, is picked from that room's hotspots.
choose: Hotspot.Arrive At:choice = Apple Tree
expectvalue: Back Door.Hotspot.ArriveAt = Apple Tree
select: Player
explain: field:InventoryBar.Combinations | Combinations | Items that go together are rows too: the two items, what they make, and what the walker says, each in a box of its own.
editorset: InventoryBar.Combinations:line:1 = I hook a sardine on. Here, kitty.
expectvalue: Player.InventoryBar.Combinations = Fishy Rod = Fishing Rod + Sardines: I hook a sardine on. Here, kitty.

chapter: Blocks | Items, tiles and recipes
create: Empty
rename: World
add: Blocks
explain: field:Blocks.Items | Items | A block world's items were a name and a tile number a line. Now the name and the tile have boxes of their own, with the tile's picture beside it.
click: editor:Blocks.Items:add
editorset: Blocks.Items:item:1 = Stone
editorset: Blocks.Items:tile:1 = 2
expectvalue: World.Blocks.Items = Stone 2
add: Crafting
explain: field:Crafting.Recipes | Recipes | A recipe says what it makes and how many, what it takes, and the workbench it needs. What it takes is a list of parts to add and take away.
click: editor:Crafting.Recipes:add
editorset: Crafting.Recipes:makes:1 = Torch
editorset: Crafting.Recipes:count:1 = 4
choose: Crafting.Recipes:takes:1:add = Sardines
click: editor:Crafting.Recipes:part:1:remove
expectvalue: World.Crafting.Recipes = Torch 4 = Sardines

chapter: Strategy and rhythm | Costs, keys and difficulties
create: Empty
rename: Knight
add: Unit
explain: field:Unit.Cost | Cost | A unit's cost is resources and how much of each, a row a resource.
editorset: Unit.Cost:count:1 = 75
expectvalue: Knight.Unit.Cost = 75 Gold
explain: field:Unit.Hotkey | Hotkey | Its hotkey is picked from the letters.
choose: Unit.Hotkey:choice = K
expectvalue: Knight.Unit.Hotkey = K
create: Empty
rename: Lanes
add: Note Lanes
explain: field:NoteLanes.Difficulty | Difficulty | The difficulty note lanes play is picked from the ones the charts have, and their colors are rows of colors to set.
choose: NoteLanes.Difficulty:difficulty:1:pick = Hard
expectvalue: Lanes.NoteLanes.Difficulty = Hard
editorset: NoteLanes.Colors:color:1 = #FFFFFF
expectvalue: Lanes.NoteLanes.Colors = #FFFFFF #F2BC4B #4BC4F2 #9A72F2

chapter: Fighters and pinball | Ticks and a compass
create: Training Pair
select: Dummy
add: Computer Fighter
explain: field:FightingCharacter.Moves | Moves | A fighter's moves show with their inputs as arrows and their frames, the Move List a click away.
explain: field:ComputerFighter.Use Moves | Use Moves | The moves the computer uses are ticked from the fighter's own.
click: editor:ComputerFighter.Use Moves:tick:Palm
expectvalue: Dummy.ComputerFighter.UseMoves = Palm
create: Empty
rename: Kicker
add: Bumper
explain: field:Bumper.Direction | Direction | A bumper's direction is turned with it, and its compass has a middle too: no direction, knocking things straight away from it, as a pop bumper does.
click: editor:Bumper.Direction:way:Up
expectvalue: Kicker.Bumper.Direction.Y = 1
click: editor:Bumper.Direction:way:None
expectvalue: Kicker.Bumper.Direction.Y = 0
say: Every one of these is an undo step, and agents get the same choices through the editor's tools.
